>> servings: 16
>> source: https://madensverden.dk/foedselsdagsboller-med-smoer-og-soedmaelk

Melt @butter{125%g} over low heat in a small #saucepan{}. Take it off the heat and add @milk{2 1/2%dl}. The mixture should be hand-warm, around 35-37 °C; if it got too hot, let it cool a little.

Pour the mixture into the #stand mixer{} bowl and dissolve @yeast{50%g} in the liquid. Add @egg{1}, @sugar{45%g} and @cardamom{1/2%tsp}, and stir the ingredients together.

Add @wheat flour{500%g} and @salt{1%tsp}. Knead with the dough hook at low to medium speed for ~knead{8%minutes}, until the dough is smooth, supple and still soft.

Cover the bowl and let the dough rise in a warm spot for ~rise{25%minutes}, until visibly risen.

Turn the dough out onto a lightly floured surface. Gently gather it and divide it into equal pieces of about 65 g.

Fold the edges of each piece toward the middle. Turn the seam side down and roll it into a round bun with a smooth, taut surface.

Place the buns on a #baking sheet{} lined with baking paper, spaced apart. Cover them with a clean tea towel and let them proof for ~proof{30%minutes}.

Meanwhile, preheat the #oven{} to 200 °C (fan) or 220 °C (conventional).

Whisk together @egg wash egg{1}, @water{1%tbsp} and @salt{1%pinch}. Gently brush the risen buns so the air isn't pressed out.

Bake the buns for ~bake{10%minutes} to 12 minutes, until evenly golden. Check on them from 10 minutes, since ovens heat differently.

Transfer the buns to a wire rack and let them cool slightly before serving.
